# Windows' git default (core.autocrlf=true, including on windows-latest
# GitHub Actions runners) checks text files out with CRLF. Several tools
# in this repo compare freshly-generated content (always \n) against a
# file read straight off disk with strict string equality --
# tools/generate-vocabulary.js's --check mode is one -- so a CRLF
# checkout makes that comparison fail unconditionally, with no real
# content drift involved. Force LF everywhere so a checkout is
# byte-identical on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary/generated assets some checkout might otherwise try to normalize.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.vsix binary
*.exe binary
*.deb binary
*.rpm binary
*.tar.gz binary
